# L1 B001 — INSTRUCTION_MAP.md, agents/code-reviewer.md, capabilities/architecture/*
1 IA m=M | Direction of conformance between instruction levels.
2 IA m=M | Placement of content by stability level.
3 IA m=M | Instruction-system structure.
  t: changing an instruction artifact
  e: NONE
4 IA m=M | Map completeness.
5 IA m=M | Neutrality of Core and Architecture wording.
6 IA m=M | Capability topology of the instruction system.
7 IA m=M rel=ARC-020,DEP-009 | Static capability composition.
8 IA m=M | Header format of instruction artifacts.
9 IA m=M | Instruction checker run.
10 IA m=MN | Where implementations may be named.
11 MX | A Reserved rule plus an ADR duty.
  - CO ARC-020~ DEP-002~ m=RA | Changing a capability selection replaces approved baseline technology.
  - XW m=M rel=GOV-017 | The change also requires an ADR recorded with architecture-decision.
    s: An approved selection change with no ADR: ARC-020 is satisfied; L1's rule is not.
12 IA m=M c=M | Registration form of the instruction system's hooks; the effect of onFailure is read statically (C10).
13 CO WF-010 m=MN d=WF | WF-010 read-only review; disallowedTools is the mechanism of the same duty (C3). Shell tools are not covered.
14 CO WF-010~ m=MN d=WF | Same mechanism; the shell gap is a coverage fact.
  t: code-reviewer agent (on delegation)
  e: NONE
15 CO WF-010 | Restates WF-010.
16 CO WF-007~ d=WF | Risk-scoped security check.
17 CO WF-001~ WF-010~ c=M | Apply the governing rules in an independent context.
18 CD WF-012~ m=M k=W c=M rel=WF-010 | The no-findings statement and unverifiable areas are WF-012; the order is the remainder.
  x: findings are returned ordered by severity
  s: Meaningful findings grouped by file: WF-012 is satisfied; L1's output format is not.
19 IA m=M | Leak rule of the capability model.
20 IA m=M | Content ownership in the capability model.
21 IA m=M | Frame and leaf ownership.
22 IA m=M | Slot contract completeness.
23 IA m=M | Slot contract content.
24 IA m=M rel=ARC-020,GOV-017 | Frame contract.
  t: creating or replacing the architecture frame
  e: NONE
25 IA m=M | Frame contract.
26 XW m=M rel=ARC-020,DEP-002,GOV-017 | ADR recording; approval is at FG-L1-6855e004e8.
  s: An approved selection change with no ADR: ARC-020 is satisfied; L1's rule is not.
27 MX | Same split as COR-M1-0002: replacing baseline technology is in ARC-020; clearing the optional frontend is not.
  - CO ARC-020~ DEP-002~ GOV-017~ m=RA | Changing the frame, replacing a leaf implementation or changing the database provider is Reserved.
  - XP m=RA rel=ARC-020,DEP-014 | Clearing the optional frontend is Reserved.
    s: A backend-only project with no frontend requirement drops the frontend module: DEP-014 fixes the stack when a frontend exists, and ARC-020 does not list it; L1 requires approval.
28 IA m=M | Replacement and removal procedure for modules.
29 IA m=M rel=ARC-020 | Replacement procedure for modules.
30 IA m=M rel=GOV-017,ARC-020 | Replacement procedure for the frame.
  t: replacing the architecture frame
  e: NONE
31 CO DEP-024~ m=MN sr=PC d=WF c=M | DEP-024 says 'do not create a separate top-level tests directory'; the checker is the mechanism (C3).
32 CO ARC-001~ m=M d=WF | Check of the inward matrix; a production project referencing a test project breaks it.
33 CO ARC-002~ ARC-008~ m=M d=WF c=M rel=ARC-028 | Framework reference ban in inner roles. Name-pattern mapping is how the check finds roles and adds no duty.
  t: backend project files when the architecture check runs
  e: NONE
34 CO ARC-001 | Restates ARC-001.
35 CO ARC-002~ ARC-008~ m=M d=WF | Mechanism of the transport-type ban (C3).
36 CO ARC-028~ m=S st=W sr=AM d=WF | Warning mechanism for ARC-028.
37 CO ARC-009~ m=S st=W sr=AM d=WF | Advisory flag for mediator packages.
38 CO ARC-009~ ARC-020~ m=RA d=WF | Mediator packages need approval; the hook reports them.
39 CO ARC-027~ m=MN | No directories without real code.
40 CO ARC-027 | Restates ARC-027.
41 CD DEP-024 DEP-013~ m=D sr=SL k=P c=M | Same reading as L0: the layout restates DEP-024; the location of frontend tests is the remainder. The DECIDED link is secondary.
  x: frontend tests stay inside the frontend workspace
  s: Frontend E2E tests in frontend/e2e, outside the workspace: DEP-024 is satisfied; L1's layout is not.
42 CO ARC-005~ ARC-004~ m=MN | No DDD directories without an approved design.
43 CO ARC-023~ | Application registers what it owns.
44 XP m=D rel=ARC-027,DEP-024 | Role folder names are layout examples (EXC-004).
  s: A repository names its folder Application/Ports: ARC-007 and DEP-024 are satisfied; L1's layout is not followed.
45 CO ARC-023~ | Api is the composition root.
46 XP m=D rel=ARC-027,RUN-024 | Type-role suffixes are naming heuristics (EXC-004).
  t: naming supporting types
  e: NONE
  s: A repository without a convention names a type TaskWorkflow: RUN-009 is satisfied; L1's guidance is not.
47 CO ARC-027~ m=SN st=W sr=GR | 'Avoid' wording of ARC-027's generic buckets.
48 XP m=D rel=RUN-009 | Same heuristics (EXC-004).
  s: As for FG-L1-915a5b7cd9.
49 CO ARC-023~ | Infrastructure registers what it owns.
50 XP m=D rel=ARC-027 | Directory shape (EXC-004).
  s: Adapters in a flat Services folder: ARC-027 is satisfied; L1's guidance is not followed.
51 XP m=MN c=M rel=ARC-012 | ARC-012 sets the composition root and does not limit extraction.
  s: Service setup is moved to an extension solely to shorten Program.cs: ARC-012 is satisfied; L1's guidance is not.
52 CO ARC-023~ ARC-012~ | Program.cs calls the layer registrations.
53 CO ARC-012 | Restates ARC-012.
54 CO ARC-001 | The matrix of ARC-001.
55 XP m=D rel=ARC-028,ARC-027,TST-002 | Same reading as M and L0: a default test-project set; the references are stated as typical.
  s: A solution tests through a single project with narrow references at the useful level: TST-002 and ARC-028 are satisfied; L1's set is not.
56 CD DEP-024~ m=D k=P c=M | Same reading as L0.
  x: frontend tests stay inside the frontend workspace
  s: As for FG-L1-124e24d760.
57 CO ARC-027~ m=D st=W sr=GR c=M rel=TST-002 | Declarative form; the reported MUST NOT is not accepted (A1).
